// A block the file never closes.
//
// Parse stage, and one diagnostic on its own. The condition is the end of the
// source: parseBlockEnd reports it on reaching the EOF token with a block
// still open, so there is exactly one per file and it has to be last. Recovery
// consumes everything after the unclosed brace, so nothing else could share
// the file anyway.
//
// The diagnostic is positioned at the EOF token, which lands on the annotation
// line below when the file has no trailing newline and on the line after it
// when it does -- so which line it is depends on a byte no editor shows you.
// The runner matches an annotation on the final line against either, so this
// file is ordinary and nothing breaks if a tool appends a newline to it.
//
// The annotation carries no column on purpose: the column is the end of the
// annotation's own text, so writing it down would make the expectation depend
// on its own length, and bless would then chase itself.

fn neverClosed() i32 {
  imm a = 1
  a
//~ ErrorNoRCurly "Expected end of block"
